# Version control and agent scratch. This checkout carries 11 G of it on disk —
# .dev 7.3 G, .claude 2.7 G, .svamp 626 M, .git 50 M — against 2.6 M of source.
#
# It is NOT 11 G of transfer. BuildKit's local source does an incremental
# filesync: it walks the context for metadata, then sends only the paths the
# COPY instructions reference. Measured on a --no-cache worker build:
# `transferring context: 2.32MB`, which is bioengine/ plus the four named
# files. Full-context tarring is the legacy builder's behaviour. What this
# saves is the metadata walk over 11 G of paths, not bandwidth.
#
# The stronger reason is robustness. Nothing here reaches an image today only
# because worker.Dockerfile and datasets.Dockerfile COPY named paths rather
# than `COPY . .`. Agent transcripts can contain credentials, so that selective
# COPY is load-bearing — and this file makes it a property of the context
# instead of a property of two Dockerfiles nobody is required to keep careful.
#
# .git is safe to exclude: the version is a static literal in pyproject.toml,
# there is no setuptools-scm, and the `git` in worker.Dockerfile is apt-get
# installing the binary rather than reading this repo.
.git/
.dev/
.claude/
.svamp/
